<script>
import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Example from '#src/lib/Example.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'

import CheckBeforeSending from './lib/CheckBeforeSending.abide'
import checkBeforeSending from './lib/CheckBeforeSending.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import MarkWhatChanged from './lib/MarkWhatChanged.abide'
import markWhatChanged from './lib/MarkWhatChanged.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import RefusedByTheServer from './lib/RefusedByTheServer.abide'
import refusedByTheServer from './lib/RefusedByTheServer.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import SavedIsTheNewStart from './lib/SavedIsTheNewStart.abide'
import savedIsTheNewStart from './lib/SavedIsTheNewStart.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import UndoAnEdit from './lib/UndoAnEdit.abide'
import undoAnEdit from './lib/UndoAnEdit.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import WaitOnTheCall from './lib/WaitOnTheCall.abide'
import waitOnTheCall from './lib/WaitOnTheCall.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import WhatASaveChanges from './lib/WhatASaveChanges.abide'
import whatASaveChanges from './lib/WhatASaveChanges.abide' with { type: 'text' }
</script>

<Doc
    seeAlso={[
        '/handlers/rpc',
        '/helpers/json-schema',
        '/helpers/refuse',
        '/browser/outbox',
    ]}
    tests={[
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/deals/lib/NewDeal.test.ts',
            from: [
                'test("a deal that does not fit shows field by field what the handler\'s refusal says"',
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/deals/lib/NewDeal.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('a refused submit moves focus to the first field with a message'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/deals/lib/NewDeal.test.ts',
            from: ["test('an edit checks the form again'"],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/deals/lib/NewDeal.test.ts',
            from: ["test('the form posts to the handler where no script runs'"],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/deals/lib/EditDeal.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('an edit marks the field it changed and the deal unsaved'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/deals/lib/EditDeal.test.ts',
            from: ["test('undo puts the deal back as it opened'"],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/deals/lib/EditDeal.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('a save makes what was saved the deal an undo goes back to'",
            ],
        },
    ]}
>
    <Section level={3} title="Check a new deal before it is sent">
        <p>The fields are read off the form as a post carries them and checked against the
            handler's own <code>jsonSchema</code>, so a deal that does not fit is refused in the
            browser with the message the server would answer. Focus goes to the first field with
            a message, and an edit checks the form again. With no script, the same form posts to
            the handler.</p>
        <Example code={checkBeforeSending} server="headless/form/lib/CheckBeforeSending.server.ts"><CheckBeforeSending /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Show a name the server refuses beside its field">
        <p>What only the server can know, it refuses with <code>refuse.validation</code>, and the
            form shows that beside the field it names as it shows its own check.</p>
        <Example code={refusedByTheServer} server="headless/form/lib/RefusedByTheServer.server.ts"><RefusedByTheServer /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Hold the button while the deal saves">
        <p><code>submit</code> is disabled while the call is in flight, and a second submit makes
            no second call.</p>
        <Example code={waitOnTheCall} server="headless/form/lib/WaitOnTheCall.server.ts"><WaitOnTheCall /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Mark the fields an edit changed">
        <p>A field's baseline is the value the page renders it with. A field typed away from it
            carries <code>data-changed</code>, and the form reads <code>dirty</code> until every
            field is back. A field rendered with no value and one cleared are the same.</p>
        <Example code={markWhatChanged} server="headless/form/lib/MarkWhatChanged.server.ts"><MarkWhatChanged /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Undo an edit back to the deal as it opened">
        <p><code>reset</code> is a reset button, disabled until something differs. It works
            with no script, since the browser's own reset restores the rendered values.</p>
        <Example code={undoAnEdit} server="headless/form/lib/UndoAnEdit.server.ts"><UndoAnEdit /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Start again from what was saved">
        <p>Once a save is answered, what it sent is the new baseline: the form reads clean, and
            Undo goes back to the saved name. A refused save moves nothing.</p>
        <Example code={savedIsTheNewStart} server="headless/form/lib/SavedIsTheNewStart.server.ts"><SavedIsTheNewStart /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="See what a save would change">
        <p><code>changes</code> holds the args a submit would send, only those whose field
            differs, coerced as the call would carry them.</p>
        <Example code={whatASaveChanges} server="headless/form/lib/WhatASaveChanges.server.ts"><WhatASaveChanges /></Example>
    </Section>
</Doc>
